2.3. Real-data vs. pseudo-data
The covariation method aims to estimate the core DEB parameters from real data, i.e. empirical observations of physiological processes. However, the estimation procedure may be guided by prior knowledge of parameter values, not unlike the concept of a “prior” in Bayesian parameter estimation methods. Conceptually, this prior knowledge is
